{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Remove the alien elohim.</b> Which you took from Shechem — even though their worshippers nullified them involuntarily, like the women of Shechem, as the Sages said: גּוֹי מְבַטֵּל עֲבוֹדָה זָרָה בְּעַל כָּרְחוֹ, 'a gentile nullifies idolatry involuntarily' (Avodah Zarah 52b–53a) — and they are therefore permitted for use. Nevertheless, remove them from your midst now, as we go to Bethel, in order that every thought of idolatry be far from your hearts."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "The Talmudic citation עבודה זרה מג., נב. refers to folios in tractate Avodah Zarah; the page reference likely spans 52b–53a based on the content and the abbreviated citation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:20.349607407Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}